1. Profile Engine

Stores stable user data.

UserProfile {
  birthChart
  elementalMix
  dominantPlanets
  goals
  values
  recurringPatterns
  preferredIntensity
  responsePreferences
}

Purpose: know who the user is.

2. Mythos Engine

Turns profile data into symbolic language.

Mythos {
  coreArchetype
  daimonicTask
  elementalStrengths
  elementalShadows
  planetaryCouncil
  currentChapter
}

Purpose: give the user a living symbolic self-map.

3. Goal Engine

Defines what the user claims to be serving.

Goal {
  id
  name
  type: "creative" | "spiritual" | "career" | "body" | "relationship"
  whyItMatters
  concreteCommitment
  avoidedThreshold
}

Purpose: prevent vague self-analysis.

4. Event Log Engine

Tracks what actually happened.

EventLog {
  date
  linkedGoalId
  plannedAction
  actualAction
  completed
  mood
  notes
  tags
}

Purpose: reality-check the myth.

5. Pattern Engine

Finds repeated contradictions.

Pattern {
  type: "avoidance" | "inflation" | "projection" | "discipline_gap" | "bypass"
  evidence
  frequency
  linkedGoals
  confidence
}

Purpose: detect the user’s real shadow from behavior.

6. Shadow Engine

Generates the uncomfortable question.

ShadowPrompt {
  mode: "mirror" | "saturn" | "daimon" | "socratic"
  evidence
  interpretation
  question
  integrationTask
}

Purpose: confront the gap between claimed values and actual behavior.

Example:

You say this project matters, but the last four logs show research replacing output. What feeling are you avoiding by not making the thing visible?

7. Calibration Engine

Learns what kind of response works.

Calibration {
  promptId
  userRating
  labels: ["useful", "too_harsh", "too_soft", "accurate", "made_me_act"]
  selectedBestResponse
}

Purpose: personalize confrontation style.

8. Response Mode Engine

Chooses how to speak.

ResponseMode {
  name: "Mirror" | "Saturn" | "Daimon" | "Socratic" | "Ritual"
  intensity: 1-5
  styleRules
}

Purpose: same insight, different delivery.